# ---- private: never commit, never deploy -------------------------------
# This repo is PUBLIC (github.com/sites-9400/NY2026). Anything here is
# world-readable and search-indexed, so keep personal records out of it.

# Booking confirmations, tickets, bank statements. These contain booking
# references, passport data and account numbers. Keep them local + Dropbox.
*/bookings/

# The Hong Kong archive: itemised spend, MariBank/Wise balances and the
# transfers between Gamaliel and Jude. Stays local + Dropbox, never pushed.
2026-07-HongKong/
**/statement_*.pdf
**/*Confirmation*.pdf
**/*confirmation*.pdf
**/*boarding*
**/*passport*

# ---- deploy-only: served from public/ but never committed ----------------
# Check-in QR codes and the booking references they encode. These ARE on the
# published page, which was a deliberate call: having them on the phone at the
# airport beats the exposure of an unlisted noindex URL. GitHub is a different
# matter, since it is public AND indexed, so they stop here.
#
# A QR encodes only the booking reference, so the code and the reference are one
# secret, not two. That is why the references are in checkin.js rather than
# written into index.html.
#
# Consequence: a fresh clone will not have these files, and the Check-in codes
# block on the Siargao page renders a fallback line instead of the cards.
# Firebase Hosting serves from public/ on disk, so the live page is unaffected.
# The originals are in 2026-08-Siargao/bookings/.
public/*/img/qr-*.png
public/*/checkin.js

